      "output": "```json\n{\n  \"scenes\": {\n    \"cloudtown\": {\n      \"bg\": \"town\",\n      \"lines\": [\n        { \"who\": \"Narrator\", \"text\": \"Above the sea of clouds hangs Mistwell Town, where lanterns drift like slow stars and every traveler carries a secret.\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Yunchuan\", \"text\": \"Three winters now, this cold has lived in my chest. Each breath feels like swallowing frost.\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Narrator\", \"text\": \"An old herb seller studies his pale face, then lowers her voice beneath the singing wind chimes.\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Narrator\", \"text\": \"'No medicine in the mortal world can thaw that frost. Only the masters of Kunlun know its name.'\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Yunchuan\", \"text\": \"Kunlun, beyond the last bridge of cloud. Then I will walk until the bridge itself runs out.\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Narrator\", \"text\": \"As he leaves, a white fox watches from a rooftop, its eyes bright as two drops of moonlight.\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Yunchuan\", \"text\": \"Strange. I could swear something followed me out of town, soft as falling snow.\" }\n      ],\n      \"next\": \"kunlun\"\n    },\n    \"kunlun\": {\n      \"bg\": \"temple\",\n      \"lines\": [\n        { \"who\": \"Narrator\", \"text\": \"The Kunlun temple stands on a peak of jade, its bells silent, its incense burning without smoke.\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Narrator\", \"text\": \"The abbot does not rise. He only opens his eyes, and the cold in Yunchuan's chest flares in answer.\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Yunchuan\", \"text\": \"Master, I have come far. Tell me how this frost may be cured, and I will pay any price.\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Narrator\", \"text\": \"'Any price? Then hear it. Your cure is the heart pearl of a nine-tailed fox in Qingqiu.'\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Yunchuan\", \"text\": \"A living heart? You would have me kill so that I may keep breathing?\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Narrator\", \"text\": \"'I ask nothing. I only tell the truth. What you do with it is the measure of your sword.'\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Yunchuan\", \"text\": \"Then I will go to Qingqiu, and decide when I meet her eyes.\" }\n      ],\n      \"next\": \"foxforest\"\n    },\n    \"foxforest\": {\n      \"bg\": \"forest\",\n      \"lines\": [\n        { \"who\": \"Narrator\", \"text\": \"The forest of Qingqiu glows with blue fire flowers. Among the trees, a song rises, older than the mountains.\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Bailing\", \"text\": \"You walk loudly for a swordsman, Yunchuan. The whole forest heard your heartbeat from the cloud bridge.\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Yunchuan\", \"text\": \"You know my name. You were the white fox on the rooftop.\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Bailing\", \"text\": \"I am Bailing. I have watched you since the town. Your cold smells of the north wind, and of loneliness.\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Narrator\", \"text\": \"Nine silver tails unfold behind her like a moonlit fan. At her breast, a pearl pulses with warm light.\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Yunchuan\", \"text\": \"The abbot said that pearl would save me. He did not say it would be yours.\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Bailing\", \"text\": \"He never tells the whole truth. Without it, I fade like mist at dawn. With it, you live.\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Bailing\", \"text\": \"Yet there is another way. Share my warmth for one year in Qingqiu, and the frost may melt.\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Yunchuan\", \"text\": \"May. A hope against a certainty. My hand rests on my sword, and my heart will not stay still.\" },\n        { \"who\": \"Narrator\", \"text\": \"The wind stills. The fire flowers bow. Bailing waits, unafraid, as though she already knows his answer, and forgives it.\" }\n      ],\n      \"choice\": [\n        { \"text\": \"Lower the sword and stay in Qingqiu with Bailing\", \"to\": \"ending_stay\" },\n        { \"text\": \"Draw the sword and take the heart pearl\", \"to\": \"ending_pearl\" }\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"endings\": {\n    \"ending_stay\": {\n      \"title\": \"The Year of Warm Snow\",\n      \"text\": \"Yunchuan sheathed his sword. Through four seasons Bailing sang beside him, and the frost in his chest melted like spring ice. When the year ended, he no longer wished to leave. In Qingqiu, they say snow still falls warm wherever the swordsman and the white fox walk together.\"\n    },\n    \"ending_pearl\": {\n      \"title\": \"The Pearl and the Empty Forest\",\n      \"text\": \"The blade fell, and Bailing did not flee. The pearl was warm in his palm, and the frost left him at last. Yet every breath now tasted of fire flowers. Yunchuan lived long and walked far, but he never again heard a song older than the mountains.\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```"
